<description>The remote CentOS Linux 7 host has packages installed that are affected by a vulnerability as referenced in the RHSA-2021:0024 advisory.

  - ImageMagick before 6.9.11-40 and 7.x before 7.0.10-40 mishandles the -authenticate option, which allows     setting a password for password-protected PDF files. The user-controlled password was not properly     escaped/sanitized and it was therefore possible to inject additional shell commands via coders/pdf.c.
    (CVE-2020-29599)

Note that Nessus has not tested for this issue but has instead relied only on the application&apos;s self-reported version number.</description>
