<description>The remote CentOS Linux 7 host has a package installed that is affected by a vulnerability as referenced in the RHSA-2021:0808 advisory.

  - A vulnerability was discovered in how p2p/p2p_pd.c in wpa_supplicant before 2.10 processes P2P (Wi-Fi     Direct) provision discovery requests. It could result in denial of service or other impact (potentially     execution of arbitrary code), for an attacker within radio range. (CVE-2021-27803)

Note that Nessus has not tested for this issue but has instead relied only on the application&apos;s self-reported version number.</description>
