<description>The remote CentOS Linux 7 host has packages installed that are affected by a vulnerability as referenced in the RHSA-2022:5162 advisory.

  - A flaw was found in PostgreSQL. There is an issue with incomplete efforts to operate safely when a     privileged user is maintaining another user&apos;s objects. The Autovacuum, REINDEX, CREATE INDEX, REFRESH     MATERIALIZED VIEW, CLUSTER, and pg_amcheck commands activated relevant protections too late or not at all     during the process. This flaw allows an attacker with permission to create non-temporary objects in at     least one schema to execute arbitrary SQL functions under a superuser identity. (CVE-2022-1552)

Note that Nessus has not tested for this issue but has instead relied only on the application&apos;s self-reported version number.</description>
