<description>The remote CentOS Linux 7 host has packages installed that are affected by a vulnerability as referenced in the RHSA-2022:8900 advisory.

  - Integer underflow in grub_net_recv_ip4_packets; A malicious crafted IP packet can lead to an integer     underflow in grub_net_recv_ip4_packets() function on rsm-&gt;total_len value. Under certain circumstances the     total_len value may end up wrapping around to a small integer number which will be used in memory     allocation. If the attack succeeds in such way, subsequent operations can write past the end of the     buffer. (CVE-2022-28733)

Note that Nessus has not tested for this issue but has instead relied only on the application&apos;s self-reported version number.</description>
