<description>The remote CentOS Linux 7 host has packages installed that are affected by a vulnerability as referenced in the RHSA-2023:7783 advisory.

  - A flaw was found in PostgreSQL that allows authenticated database users to execute arbitrary code through     missing overflow checks during SQL array value modification. This issue exists due to an integer overflow     during array modification where a remote user can trigger the overflow by providing specially crafted     data. This enables the execution of arbitrary code on the target system, allowing users to write arbitrary     bytes to memory and extensively read the server&apos;s memory. (CVE-2023-5869)

Note that Nessus has not tested for this issue but has instead relied only on the application&apos;s self-reported version number.</description>
